{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Mixpanel’s limits:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON array of content type "},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one object per record, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first, each with two members: "},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s "},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is, and "},{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s stored properties by name, then these members:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; left out for a record with no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds it; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0\""},{"type":"text","text":", so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The project token","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", and no other device"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier. Mixpanel counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so its unique users are sessions. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its own anonymous user, linked to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing, rather than an event with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which Mixpanel would attribute to no user,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or to a hash of the request’s address. Mixpanel treats two events of the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" as one, so a recovered record that Mixpanel had already stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under its session, before the app ended, is stored again. The record’s vendor identifier and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Mixpanel cuts each string down to 255 characters. It drops an event of 255 properties or more,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"counting the members above and the default properties below, one holding an array of 255","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements or more, and one whose property nests objects more than 3 deep, though it answers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"200: the encoder enforces these limits, leaving such a record out of the request.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" also holds Mixpanel’s default properties, named as its Swift SDK names them, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version_string"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build_number"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The version and build, each left out when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$model","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The model","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$wifi","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The operating system’s name and version","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ do, one with a property named as one Mixpanel reads for itself,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one past Mixpanel’s limits on properties, array elements or nesting, one whose event isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"text":" Mixpanel takes, and one too large for Mixpanel (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" logs and reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. Mixpanel answers a request it reads with 200, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" retries one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400, 401 or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"413. Mixpanel answers 200 as well when it ingests none of a request’s events: a wrong region,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or a token of no project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored, so check the project’s Live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"View after setting it up. Its track API ingests only events from the last 5 days: a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"older than that when it is sent, such as one a store kept through a long time offline, is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counted as delivered and not stored. A record sent again keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same for the same records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/track"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/init(projectToken:plan:limit:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"generated":true},{"title":"Type Properties","anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder"}],"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift#L83","fileName":"MixpanelBatchEncoder.swift"},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct"},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" sends."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","title":"BatchEncoder","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"HTTPDestination","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as the requests its encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits it into, and sends each again until it arrives."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror","kind":"symbol","title":"MixpanelEncodingError","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"MixpanelEncoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"batchLimit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel’s limits on one request: 2,000 event